# JobPilot production environment (example)

Copy values into the process environment for `npm start` (or your process manager). Never commit real secrets.

```bash
NODE_ENV=production
PORT=3000

# Session cookies on HTTPS
COOKIE_SECURE=1

# Admin MFA stays disabled for now. Do not set REQUIRE_ADMIN_MFA=1 until you choose to require it.
# REQUIRE_ADMIN_MFA=0
# Optional first-boot admin (only used when DB has no admin yet)
# ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@example.com
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=replace-me-strong

# Optional SMTP overrides (Admin → Email can also store these)
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.com
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_SECURE=false
# SMTP_USER=
# SMTP_PASSWORD=
# SMTP_FROM=hello@example.com

# Interview rooms
# STUN_URIS=stun:stun.l.google.com:19302
# TURN_URIS=turn:turn.example.com:3478?transport=udp
# TURN_USERNAME=jobpilot
# TURN_CREDENTIAL=replace-me

# Optional match embeddings
# MATCH_EMBEDDINGS=0
```

See also: `deploy/HTTPS.md`, `deploy/turn.env.example`, `docs/LAUNCH_CHECKLIST.md`.
